# 4. TEXT

_publ_section_synopsis
;
Rietveld refinement of a new zinc divanadate, Zn~3~(OH)~2~V~2~O~7~.2H~2~O, 
shows that it has a porous framework structure assembled from layers of 
Zn--O octahedra joined by pyrovanadate groups. Water molecules fill the 
large cavities.
;

_publ_section_abstract                           
; Hydrothermally prepared zinc dihydroxide divanadate dihydrate crystallizes 
in the trigonal system (space group P\=3m1). Its structure was solved ...
;

_publ_section_comment
; Recently, mild hydrothermal reactions driven by template cations
such as ...
;
_publ_section_exptl_prep     
; The title compound was prepared by hydrothermal treatment of ZnCl~2~,
V~2~O~5~ and tetramethylammonium hydroxide, [N(CH~3~)~4~]OH, in a 1:1:3 
molar ratio at pH = 5.6. The reaction mixture was heated in a Teflon-lined 
Parr reactor for 2.5 d at 438 K. White crystalline powder resulted.
;

_publ_section_exptl_refinement  
;
The powder diffraction pattern was indexed in a hexagonal system ...
;
_publ_section_references   
;
Akselrud, L. G., Zavalij, P. Y., Grin, Yu. N., Pecharskii, V. K., 
Baumgartner, B. & Wolfel, E. (1993). Mater. Sci. Forum, 133/136, 335-340.

Basso, R., Palenzona, A. & Zefiro, L. (1988). Neues Jahrb. Miner. 
pp. 385-394.

...

;
_publ_section_figure_captions
; Fig. 1. Polyhedral representation of Zn~3~(OH)~2~V~2~O~7~.2H~2~O.

Fig. 2. Comparison of observed (circles) and calculated (solid line) 
intensities for Zn~3~(OH)~2~V~2~O~7~.2H~2~O. The difference pattern 
appears below.
;
_publ_section_acknowledgements
; The work at Binghamton was supported by the National Science Foundation
through grant DMR 9422667.
;

